group: C2v
formula: NO2
construction: a central atom and its neighbours
headline: 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · not drawn: O2 internal: 3 levels, 6 e; tick Show all levels · labels in C<sub>2v</sub>\n2 high empty levels drawn at the top (true energy beside them)
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (N and O2). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the column on the right, on its own energy axis in Hartree and to scale. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, at its calculated energy, in the colour of the model level it matches. A level marked ≈ matches only loosely (overlap below 0.80; the value is in the hover text). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\nThe model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order. Virtual orbitals above the LUMO depend strongly on the basis set.\n\n**Total electrons: 17** (N 5, O2 12).\n\nThe levels counted in the note under the diagram are model levels that sit almost entirely on the O2 and take no part in the interaction; they are counted, not drawn.\n\n**Caveats.** 2 high empty levels drawn at the top (true energy beside them). Extended Hückel puts empty antibonding orbitals tens of eV up, so an empty level more than 30 eV above the HOMO is drawn at the top of the axis with its model energy written beside it, or not at all when it sits almost entirely on one fragment. A loose match means no calculated orbital resembles the model level closely; read its calculated energy with care.\n\n**Unrestricted calculation.** This is an unrestricted calculation: the levels are drawn at their alpha energies, and the beta electrons are matched to them by symmetry.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in C2v; the code reported none.  b1 and b2 (b2 and b3 in D2h) depend on the choice of axes; ECCE follows Mulliken's convention, as most textbooks do.
verdict: ok The model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order.
